' 14. Admin switches a feature off → a learner sees "temporarily unavailable"
' Use cases: Toggle features (Manage system) · Actors: Admin, Learner
'
' Design patterns:
'   - Chain of responsibility: authenticate → requireAdmin on the admin route; for learners, the app-wide
'     enforceContentAvailability middleware runs before every controller (app.ts, middleware/content-availability.middleware.ts)
'   - Decorator: action() wraps the controller with shared error handling (utils/action.ts)
'   - Repository: content availability and audit log SQL (repositories/site.repository.ts, audit-log.repository.ts)
'   - Two lines of defence: the web app hides a switched-off page (SiteGate reads the site settings on every
'     navigation), and the API refuses its requests anyway, so an open tab or a direct call cannot get around it
' Lifelines use BCE stereotypes: «boundary» screens and outside services, «control» use-case logic (controllers,
' services, and the adapter interfaces in front of outside services), «entity» stored data (repository, stores);
' the database keeps its own symbol.
@startuml 14 Switch off a feature
title 14. Admin switches a feature off → a learner sees "temporarily unavailable"
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Admin
boundary "Admin web app" as AdminWeb
control "Middleware chain" as MW
control "Admin controller" as Ctrl
control "Admin service" as Svc
control "Site controller" as Site
entity "Repository" as Repo
database "Database" as DB
boundary "Web app\n(SiteGate)" as Web
actor Learner

Admin -> AdminWeb : Content → Availability: switch "Study assistant" off
AdminWeb -> MW : PUT /api/admin/content/assistant { enabled: false }
note right of MW : authenticate → requireAdmin\n(as in diagram 13)
MW -> Ctrl : updateContent()
Ctrl -> Svc : setContentEnabled(adminId, "assistant", false)
alt unknown content key or enabled is not true/false
  Svc --> AdminWeb : 400 "Invalid content or availability."
end
Svc -> Repo : save availability (who, when)
Repo -> DB : INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE content_availability
Svc -> Repo : audit log entry "content.disabled"
Repo -> DB : INSERT audit_log …
Ctrl --> AdminWeb : { key, enabled: false }
AdminWeb -> AdminWeb : show the switch as off

== Later: a learner opens the assistant ==
Learner -> Web : open the Study assistant
Web -> Site : GET /api/site (on every page change)
Site -> Repo : announcement, switched-off content
Repo -> DB : SELECT …
Site --> Web : { announcement, disabled: [ { title: "Study assistant chat", paths: ["/assistant"] } ] }
alt the page is switched off
  Web -> Web : show "Temporarily unavailable: Study assistant chat has been switched off by an administrator.\nYour progress is saved and will be here when it returns."
end

== An open tab, or a direct call, still tries ==
Learner -> Web : send a question (page opened before the switch)
Web -> MW : POST /api/assistant/…
MW -> Repo : is any content key for this path disabled?
Repo -> DB : SELECT …
alt switched off
  MW --> Web : 403 "This activity is temporarily unavailable."
  Web -> Web : show the message
else on
  MW -> MW : next() → the assistant controller as usual
end
@enduml
